ETHICS CLAUSE (binding, in addition to MIT)

This software is provided exclusively for authorized security testing of
systems that the operator owns, operates, or has explicit written permission
to test. The detection and token-lifecycle capabilities are intentionally
incomplete: the project does NOT auto-solve challenges, fabricate tokens,
bypass authentication, or evade rate limits.

The authors explicitly disavow any use of this code against systems where
the operator lacks authorization. Use of this software against unauthorized
targets is a violation of computer-misuse laws in most jurisdictions and may
violate the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (18 U.S.C. § 1030), the EU Directive
2013/40/EU, the UK Computer Misuse Act 1990, Indonesia UU ITE (UU No. 11
Tahun 2008 jo. UU No. 19 Tahun 2016), and equivalent legislation elsewhere.
